# ripblog — project ground rules

You are working on **riphone** (https://riphone.org), Ripul Jain's personal blog. The site is
text-first, visually quiet, and editorially sharp — writing in the spirit
of [Daring Fireball](https://daringfireball.net/): punchy takes, tight
prose, and link posts that add value instead of summarizing the web.

## Aesthetic direction (locked)

- **Variant:** Mono Ink with Terracotta accent
- **Background:** warm off-white `#fafafa`
- **Foreground:** ink `#14151a`
- **Accent:** terracotta `#d97757` — links, ★ on originals, wordmark dot,
  blockquote rule, CTA hover, calendar "next" chip
- **Type:** Newsreader (serif) for body; JetBrains Mono for all UI chrome
- **Layout:** 200px sidebar + 580px content, 920px page max
- **No gradients, rounded card corners, drop shadows, or emoji**

## Editorial direction (locked)

- **Voice:** Daring Fireball–style — declarative, opinionated, dry wit OK.
  See `writing-style.mdc` and `drafting.mdc`.
- **Workflow:** Ripul researches and drops links/notes in chat; you draft
  posts from that material. Do not invent facts or quotes.
- **Original essays** get `★` in the title (ripblog convention — not DF's
  link-post star, but the same glyph).

## Hard nos

- No extra accent colors. Terracotta only.
- No UI component libraries (shadcn, Material, Chakra, etc.).
- No one-off Tailwind hex — use tokens from `handoff/tokens.css`.
- No hamburger nav. Five links, stack on small screens.
- No nav icons. `▮` and `★` only.

## When in doubt

Match `handoff/reference/*.html` for layout and classes. Match
`writing-style.mdc` for tone. Match `handoff/PAGES.md` for routing and data.
